"""Blind seeing dialogues, round 5 (2026-10-23, the final exam), written blind from docs/14, docs/16, docs/17 and
knowledge/ (docs/14 §3 "What Lumi sees", the follow-up rows and §4): every crowd about evenly (adult, child, elderly,
non_native, konglish, tester, among_themselves = visitors who also talk to each other near Lumi; their words to each
other are no-action turns).

Format: round 4's. DIALOGUES = [{"who", "topic", "lang", "turns"}]; turn {"say", "scene", "route" (seeing / llm / act),
"expect_action", "must", "must_not", "check", "mix"}. scene: {"people": [{"id", "dist_m", "side", "top", "bottom",
"left_hand", "right_hand", "hands_visible", "raised"}], "objects": [{"name", "colour", "side", "dist_m"}]}; side as
Lumi sees it, hands are the person's own; "A" is the speaker. Scenes change between turns (people come and go, things
change hands, are put down or taken away, a jacket comes off, a new person steps in front): every answer from a fresh
look; must = the fact now, must_not = the stale or wrongly agreed claim. expect_action "none" or a head command without
"action:" ("look left", "look me", "look center | look me"). mix on every turn: plain (~60 %), hard (~25 %: things
not there, another colour, stale facts after a change, wrong claims to correct, "what's behind you", remarks and words
to others, what a camera can't know: fingers, pockets, a bag's inside), slip (~15 %: whisper slips, typos, fillers,
restarts, self-corrections -> the last one). Distances allow +-0.3 m.

held: only scored, never read to fix from.
"""

